        "heading_d9yrbf": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Care Questions"
          }
        },
        "question_CAhEYF": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "default_open": false,
            "title": "How do I care for my items?",
            "content": "<p>All HEAVENLY ESSENTIALS items can be hand or machine-washed, on gentle cycle only. If using a washing machine, it must be set on delicate cycle setting. Hand washing will help to extend the life of your garment, and is also more gentle on the environment. We recommend using a wash bag in cool water and laying flat dry - reducing energy and also better for your undies longevity.</p><p>Avoid using bleach or chemical detergents. To Whiten & Brighten your Heavenlies, we recommend a bleach-free alternative, like natural Oxygen Whitener, that can be added to the wash cycle. If your garments become 'sheer' over time, we recommend washing and putting in the dryer (when damp) for 10-15 minutes, on the lowest heat setting, so the fibers can expand and thicken.</p>",
            "show_icon": false,
            "icon_name": "icon-award",
            "icon_size": 20,
            "icon_color": "#545454"
          }
        },
        "question_j7V7ea": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "default_open": false,
            "title": "Compostability?",
            "content": "<p>Heavenly Essentials underwear is a unique combination of 100% GOTS certified organic flax linen, organic linen thread, and flax/natural tree rubber elastics- making them one of the world's only compostable underwear. Please note that home compost times may vary, due to your compost's unique moisture and microbiome environment. </p><p>Heavenly Essentials underwear are 100% home and commercially compostable! Made from a unique combination of plant-based materials, our panties compost in approximately 2 weeks (temperature, microbiome compost composition dependent). Simply wash, cut up and plant in the compost! </p>",
            "show_icon": false,
            "icon_name": "icon-award",
            "icon_size": 20,
            "icon_color": "#545454"
          }
        },
        "question_jBXtVF": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "default_open": false,
            "title": "What is the lifespan of a pair?",
            "content": "<p><strong>Natural flax fibers can last up to three times longer than synthetics, cotton or other materials, making them a great investment! </strong>With gentle wash and care, <em>Heavenly Essentials are designed to be stronger and last longer than conventional clothing. </em></p><p><em>Flax is the most durable natural fiber to exist. After years of love and wear, we recommend planting them in the compost. A fully regenerative garment!</em></p>",
            "show_icon": false,
            "icon_name": "icon-award",
            "icon_size": 20,
            "icon_color": "#545454"
          }
        },
        "question_HbyeMR": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "default_open": false,
            "title": "Will HEAVENLY biodegrade on my body?",
            "content": "<p>Heavenly Essentials underwear, tees and essentials will never biodegrade while wearing or washing them. Only when your heavenlies time is up, we recommend planting them vs. throwing in the trash. Made from flax (plant-based) when planted turn back to Earth in as fast as two weeks. </p><p>In the compost, your Heavenlies will become nutrient rich soil that helps combat climate change. <a href=\"/pages/composting-at-home-guide\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Composting at Home Guide\">Read here </a>our guide on how to compost. No compost? No problem. <a href=\"/products/compost-collective-membership\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Compost Collective Membership\">Join our Compost Collective </a>Program and we will compost for you!</p>",
            "show_icon": false,
            "icon_name": "icon-award",
            "icon_size": 20,
            "icon_color": "#545454"
          }
        }
